{
 "_what": "The account routes for AI harness hooks (src/account/hooks.rs) and the command a harness config runs (the `hook APP_FILES_LIST HARNESS EVENT` command, the event JSON on stdin). Moved from the previous owner\u2019s harness/setup.json `hooks`, harness/register-session.mjs with wake-sessions.json, harness/decisions-since.mjs with decisions-since.json, and harness/record-every-message.mjs with record-every-message.json. Code names only generic steps; every harness, hook, record kind, path and word is a row here, so a new harness or hook is a row. `resource` and `operation` are the operation that takes one event: input {harness, event, payload, messages?, transcript_recorded?, executions?}; it answers {said, accepted, executions_accepted}. `records` is the generic records operations each step writes and reads through, admitted for the same caller. `client` is what the command does on this computer before and after it calls the account: the cursor folder (an entry of this computer's one home and a path inside it, src/native_entry/home.json; an entry that is not an engine row there is refused when this file is read), the time box and the read bounds of a transcript. `hooks` are the rows the account runs for an event, in order: step `keep-record` writes one record whose id and value fill {holes} from the event (session registration), of the kind the account's installed tools' record model names in `kind.section` under `kind.key` (tools/hand-work-to-ais: `harness_hooks.agent_card`; {type} is that kind; with no tool naming it the step is refused and keeps nothing); step `say-recorded` says `words.recorded_line` when the session's transcript is one a harness row here records; step `say-unseen` calls one operation with {reader} and says `words.heading` and one `- <said>` line per item it answers (the decisions since this session last looked); step `record-messages` keeps each message the command read (`from` transcript: everything new in the session's transcript since its cursor; `from` prompt: the prompt the person just submitted, kept before the AI works), as one record of `messages.type`, written only when absent so a resend is the message already kept. `harnesses` are the transcript rows of record-every-message.json (attachments and source returns are not moved yet), with `event_names`, the names each harness gives the three events. `injected_text` is record-every-message.json's, written for a regex without look-around. Optional executions are bounded observations with a transient local transcript path and exact byte occurrence, verified before protected journal capture. Paths and transcript payloads are never retained in execution records.",
 "resource": "@harness-hooks",
 "operation": "hooks:receive",
 "request_key_prefix": "hook",
 "records": {
  "resource": "@own-records",
  "read": "records:read",
  "write": "records:write"
 },
 "client": {
  "time_box_ms": 4000,
  "max_event_bytes": 1048576,
